## Final Judgement
## Summary of Key Insights
The fact-check found no credible evidence supporting the claim. No law enforcement agency confirmed child sexual abuse material on Hunter Biden’s laptop. The New York Post’s October 2020 articles mentioned “nearly 25,000 images” but described them as sexually explicit selfies and porn, not child abuse, and did not mention China or torture/rape of children. The specific allegation about child torture and rape in China was added later by fringe outlets like OAN and Revolver News, without any corroboration. No verified photographs, witness accounts, or victim testimonies exist.

## Conclusion
The claim is explicitly and clearly refuted by the evidence: the original source of the “25,000 images” story did not allege child abuse, and no credible authority or direct evidence supports the extreme details about torture and rape of children in China. Therefore, the decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
No credible law enforcement agency has confirmed child sexual abuse material on Hunter Biden’s laptop, and the original New York Post articles from October 2020 that reported “nearly 25,000 images” described them as “sexually explicit selfies and porn,” not child abuse, and did not mention China or torture/rape of children ([source](https://nationalfile.com/bombshell-ny-post-refuses-to-publish-all-25000-hunter-pics-after-reports-they-include-child-porn/)). The specific allegation about 25,000 images of torturing and raping children under 10 in China was added later by fringe outlets like OAN and Revolver News, without any corroboration ([source](https://nationalfile.com/bombshell-ny-post-refuses-to-publish-all-25000-hunter-pics-after-reports-they-include-child-porn/)). No verified photographs, witness accounts, or victim testimonies exist ([source](https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/aug/12/facebook-posts/fact-checking-pedophilia-attacks-against-joe-biden/)), and the claim has been identified as an antisemitic conspiracy theory ([source](https://www.politifact.com/search/stories/?q=farrakhan)). Therefore, the claim is refuted.